An object A of mass 100 g is moving in a straight line with a velocity of 0.60 m s⁻¹ to the right. An object B of mass 200 g is moving in the same straight line as object A with a velocity of 0.80 m s⁻¹ to the left, as shown in Fig. 4.1.
{{figure:figure_4_1.png}}
Objects A and B collide. Object A then moves with a velocity of 0.40 m s⁻¹ to the left.
